  "body": "PR1972 supplies a complete P104 `G/2` channel with arbitrary dirty helpers, but its replay assumes abstract consistent frame charts. This adds a concrete finite native realization at its pinned head `fd82d172f46933fd253c2c6de4bd5eaff5429cfd`: 740 exact Clifford transport recipes, 208 monomial intrinsic endpoint adapters, and a separate checker for the complete 280-input framed composition. The scalar channel and schedule remain credited to their authors.\n\nThe compiler first converts compressed E8 labels through their actual Gram form into physical binary labels. Independent signed-Pauli and exact Gaussian interpretation checks every primitive, including global phase, and all 4096 private-drop basis columns. The complete row induction restores all 72 arbitrary dirty helpers. Five genuine mutations reject. The profile remains **rank mass 2368 = boundary coverage 2312 + COPY56**.\n\n**No new kappa or complete P104 supplier.** The `I-G/2` side correction, chronological global ownership, recursive precision and all-size admission remain open. The selected record is unchanged. This closes a finite native-realization obligation, not those later gates.\n\nValidation at `6e222517e182e98499239bc9a4009f540e1c5520`:\n\n- Local Python 3.11.15 and 3.14.8 receipts are byte-identical; a read-only relocated export also passes complete recipe regeneration.\n- Linux CI: [all three jobs pass](https://github.com/chafreaky/integer-mult-bounds/actions/runs/38597630611) on Python 3.11, 3.12 and 3.14, including complete regeneration. All three downloaded receipts are byte-identical to the local receipts.\n- Standard-library, read-only replay: `python3 -I -O -B research/p104-native-channel/verify.py --regenerate`. Regeneration uses temporary storage and compares complete decompressed payloads. Registered package metadata and source pins pass.\n\nCredit Rohan Arun / [PR1972](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1972) for the entire scalar/frame channel, Adam Gall / [PR1940](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1940) for the schedule, Josie Elliston / PR1071 for the fixture, Ali Romman / PR1125 and PR1862, and the retained E8, dirty-helper and exact-compiler lineage. Exact input pins and inherited notices are included. Native lowering and independent checker work prepared for Chafik Boukhalfa with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no independent human review or formal proof assistant.\n",
